---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 12</p>
  <h1>Travel &amp; <em>transport</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Say how you get to work, plan a trip, and handle the airport with calm. Learn the everyday transport words, then use <strong>by + transport</strong> for how you travel and <strong>verb chunks</strong> for what you do: <span class="ex">by train</span>, <span class="ex">on foot</span>, <span class="ex">take a taxi</span>, <span class="ex">catch the bus</span>, <span class="ex">check in</span>, <span class="ex">board at the gate</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">by + transport</span>
    <span class="tag">travel verb chunks</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read a traveler’s morning message.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>by + transport, and verbs that come in chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose, type, and build travel sentences.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Talk about real trips and dream trips.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Getting around: <span class="ex">by bus</span>, <span class="ex">by train</span>, <span class="ex">by car</span>, <span class="ex">by plane</span>, or <span class="ex">on foot</span>. At the airport, the order never changes: <span class="ex">check in</span>, <span class="ex">go through security</span>, <span class="ex">find your gate</span>, <span class="ex">board</span>.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="at">at</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="went">went</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="go">go</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The bus leaves <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="at" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 7:30 in the morning. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1 lesson · prepositions of time and place)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Last summer we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="went" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to Italy by train. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A2 lesson · past simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Next month I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> going to visit my sister. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A2 lesson · be going to)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the transport</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Ways to travel and useful trip words. Say each kind of transport aloud with <span class="ex">by</span>: <span class="ex">by bus</span>, <span class="ex">by train</span>, <span class="ex">by plane</span>. For the trip words, try <span class="ex">I packed…</span> or <span class="ex">We booked…</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/airplane.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">plane</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/train.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">train</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bus.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bus</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/car.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">car</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/taxi.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">taxi</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/ship.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">ship</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/motorcycle.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">motorcycle</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/metro.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">metro</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/helicopter.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">helicopter</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bicycle.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bicycle</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/luggage.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">luggage</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/ticket.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">ticket</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/world-map.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">map</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/tent.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">camping</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/beach.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">beach</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mountain.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">mountain</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/compass.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">compass</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/hotel.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hotel</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Read the traveler’s message</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“I usually go to work <strong>by train</strong>, but today I’m <strong>taking a taxi</strong> because I have a big suitcase. My flight leaves at 9:40. I’ll <strong>check in</strong> at 7:30, <strong>go through security</strong>, and <strong>board at the gate</strong>. I really hope I don’t <strong>miss it</strong>!”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">by train</span>. There is no <span class="ex">a</span> and no <span class="ex">the</span>. Which little word comes before the transport?</li>
      <li>Now compare: <span class="ex">taking <strong>a</strong> taxi</span>, <span class="ex">miss <strong>it</strong></span>. Verbs like <span class="ex">take</span>, <span class="ex">catch</span>, and <span class="ex">miss</span> need <span class="ex">a</span> or <span class="ex">the</span>. So when do we use plain <span class="ex">by + transport</span>?</li>
      <li>Find the airport steps in the message. What does the traveler do first, next, and last?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check · read the cue, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">For how you travel, use <b>by</b> + transport with no article. Walking is <b>on foot</b>. Inside a big vehicle you are <b>on</b> it; inside a car or taxi you are <b>in</b> it.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="by">by</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I go to work <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="by" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> bus. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(how you travel · no article)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>She travels to Chicago <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="by" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> train. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(how you travel · no article)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The office is close, so I go <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> foot. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(walking · a special chunk)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Quiet, please. I’m <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bus. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(a big vehicle · you can walk inside it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>They’re <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a taxi on the way to the airport. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(a car · you sit inside it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>We never travel <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="by" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> car at night. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(how you travel · no article)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: by + transport, or on foot</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>To say <strong>how you travel in general</strong>, use <span class="ex">by</span> + transport with <strong>no article</strong>: <span class="ex">by bus, by train, by car, by plane, by metro</span>. Walking has its own chunk: <span class="ex">on foot</span>, never <span class="ex">by foot</span>.</p>
  <p>To say <strong>where you are</strong>, the vehicle matters. You are <span class="ex">on</span> big transport you can walk inside: <span class="ex">on the bus, on the train, on the plane, on the ship</span>. You are <span class="ex">in</span> a car or taxi, because you sit inside: <span class="ex">in the car, in a taxi</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>by + transport <span class="contraction">no a, no the</span></th><th>watch out</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>by bus, by train, by metro</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">not by a bus</span></td><td><b>on foot</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">= walking, not by foot</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>by plane, by ship</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">how you travel</span></td><td><b>on the bus, on the train, on the plane</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">where you are</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>by car, by taxi</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">how you travel</span></td><td><b>in the car, in a taxi</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">you sit inside</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">by</span> + transport has no article: <span class="ex">by bus</span>, not <span class="ex">by a bus</span>. But with verbs like <span class="ex">take</span>, <span class="ex">catch</span>, and <span class="ex">miss</span>, you need one: <span class="ex">take a taxi, catch the 7:15 train, miss the bus</span>.</li>
      <li>Big transport takes <span class="ex">get on / get off</span>: <span class="ex">get on the bus, get off the train</span>. Cars and taxis take <span class="ex">get in / get out of</span>: <span class="ex">get in the car, get out of the taxi</span>.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">trip</span>, <span class="ex">travel</span>, <span class="ex">journey</span>: a <span class="ex">trip</span> is one visit, there and back (<span class="ex">a business trip, a trip to Rome</span>). <span class="ex">travel</span> is the activity in general (<span class="ex">I love travel</span>, not <span class="ex">a travel</span>). A <span class="ex">journey</span> is the time you spend moving (<span class="ex">a long train journey</span>). Keep it simple: for most stories, say <span class="ex">trip</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Travel verbs come in chunks</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Learn the verb and its partner together, as one chunk: <span class="ex"><strong>catch</strong> a train</span> (arrive in time for it), <span class="ex"><strong>miss</strong> a train</span> (arrive too late), <span class="ex"><strong>take</strong> a taxi</span>, <span class="ex"><strong>book</strong> a flight</span> or <span class="ex">a hotel</span>, <span class="ex"><strong>check in</strong></span>, <span class="ex"><strong>pack</strong> a suitcase</span>, <span class="ex"><strong>get on / get off</strong> the bus</span>, <span class="ex"><strong>get in / get out of</strong> a car</span>.</p>
  <p>At the airport or the station, the sequence is always the same: <span class="ex">check in</span> → <span class="ex">go through security</span> → <span class="ex">find your gate</span> → <span class="ex">board</span>. Say the four steps aloud, in order, before you start the drill.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1 · choose the travel chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the cue in parentheses first. Each chunk fits exactly one sentence.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="catch">catch</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="miss">miss</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="take">take</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="book">book</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="check">check</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="pack">pack</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get on">get on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="get off">get off</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Hurry up! We can still <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="catch" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the 7:15 train. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= arrive in time for it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>If we don’t leave now, we’ll <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="miss" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> our flight. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= arrive too late for it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>It’s late. Let’s <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="take" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a taxi home. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= ride in it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>I want to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="book" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a flight to Denver for August. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= reserve it online)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We can <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="check" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in online 24 hours before the flight. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the first airport step)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I need to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="pack" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> my suitcase tonight. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= put your clothes inside)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>It’s cold out here. Let’s <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="get on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bus and find two seats. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= enter it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>This is our stop. We need to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="get off" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bus now. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= leave it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2 · type the missing word</h3>
    <p>One word per gap. Read the cue in parentheses, then say the full sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I was late this morning, so I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="missed" data-hint="You arrived too late for it. Use the past simple." data-fix="missed" /> the bus. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(opposite of caught · past simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We should <input class="answer-input" data-answer="book" data-hint="Reserve it online, like a hotel room." data-fix="book" /> a flight soon; July tickets are getting expensive. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(= reserve)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>At the airport, first you <input class="answer-input" data-answer="check" data-hint="It is the first airport step, before security." data-fix="check" /> in at the desk or online. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the first airport step)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Don’t forget to <input class="answer-input" data-answer="pack" data-hint="Put your clothes inside it." data-fix="pack" /> your suitcase tonight. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(clothes go inside)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>You <input class="answer-input" data-answer="get" data-hint="It pairs with on: the chunk for entering big transport." data-fix="get" /> on the bus at the front and get off at the back. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(enter big transport)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Last night we <input class="answer-input" data-answer="took" data-hint="Use the past simple of take." data-fix="took" /> a taxi from the station to the hotel. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(take · past simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the meaning, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she took a taxi to the airport">
    <h3>Drill 3 · build the trip report</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">She had a big suitcase and an early flight. Build the past simple sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="airport">airport</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="taxi">taxi</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="took">took</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="we are going to book a flight">
    <h3>Drill 4 · build the plan</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You and a friend have a summer plan. Build the sentence with <span class="ex">be going to</span>, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="flight">flight</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="going">going</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="we">We</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="book">book</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="with" data-fix="I go to work by bus." data-why="Use by + transport with no article: by bus, by train, by car.">
    <h3>Drill 5 · how do you travel?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. Think about the little word that goes with transport.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="go">go</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="work">work</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="with">with</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="bus">bus.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="off" data-fix="We got out of the taxi at the hotel." data-why="A taxi is a car you sit inside, so use get in and get out of: we got out of the taxi.">
    <h3>Drill 6 · big transport or car?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. A taxi is small; you sit inside it.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">We</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="got">got</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="off">off</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">the</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="taxi">taxi</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="at">at</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the2">the</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hotel">hotel.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 · say the travel chunk, then check</h3>
    <p>Say the full chunk or sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> a taxi &nbsp;→&nbsp; ride in it (verb + a taxi)</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>take a taxi</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> a flight &nbsp;→&nbsp; reserve it online (verb + a flight)</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>book a flight</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> the bus &nbsp;→&nbsp; enter it</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>get on the bus</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> the car &nbsp;→&nbsp; leave it</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>get out of the car</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> a suitcase &nbsp;→&nbsp; fill it with clothes (verb + a suitcase)</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>pack a suitcase</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> We catch the 7:15 train. &nbsp;→&nbsp; yesterday (past simple)</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We caught the 7:15 train.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A trip plan</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“Hi Marco! Here’s the plan for Friday. Our flight to Boston leaves at 9:40, so let’s take a taxi to the airport at 6:30. We check in at 7:00, go through security, and board at the gate at 9:10. In Boston we’ll take the metro to the hotel; it’s faster than the bus. Pack light, one small suitcase each!”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real trip plan.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="by taxi">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. How are they going to the airport?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="by taxi">by taxi</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="by metro">by metro</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="by bus">by bus</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="9:10">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What time do they board the plane?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="9:40">9:40</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="7:00">7:00</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="9:10">9:10</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="by metro">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. How are they getting to the hotel in Boston?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="by bus">by bus</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="by metro">by metro</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="by taxi">by taxi</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your daily route:</b> Say how you get to work or school, how long it takes, and what you do when the weather is bad. <span class="ex">I go to work by metro. It takes about thirty minutes. When it rains, I take a taxi.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your last trip:</b> Tell the story in the past simple: where, how, and one problem or surprise. <span class="ex">Last May I took a trip to the mountains. We went by bus, and the journey took five hours. We almost missed the bus home!</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Interview the teacher about travel, then report one answer. <span class="ex">How do you get to work? Do you ever travel by train? When was your last trip, and where did you go?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Dream trip:</b> Plan a future trip with <span class="ex">be going to</span>: the place, the transport, and two things you will do there. <span class="ex">Next year I’m going to visit Japan. I’m going to book the flights in January and travel between cities by train.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Compare two kinds of transport:</b> Choose two ways to travel in your city and compare them. Which one do you take, and why? <span class="ex">The metro is faster than the bus, but the bus goes everywhere. I usually take the metro because I hate traffic.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the system</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “To say how I travel in general, I use ______ + transport, with no article: <strong>by bus, by train</strong>. Walking is <strong>on</strong> ______. For a bus, a train, or a plane, I get on and get ______. For a car or a taxi, I get in and get ______ of.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about how you get to work and one about your next trip.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You can name everyday transport, say how you travel with by and on foot, and use travel chunks like catch a train, book a flight, check in, and get off the bus.">
    <h3>Final quiz · choose the right word</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="by">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. I usually go to work ___ train.</p>
